171},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":173,"xml:id":174,"ref":175},"Zoe Greblunas","ZG","https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0871-248X",{"_":177,"xml:id":178,"ref":179},"Marta Fogagnolo","martaf","https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163",{"_":181,"when":182,"who":183},"Marta Fogagnolo revised the text encoding, added the translation and the commentary","2026-08-03","#martaf",[],[186,187,188,189],"Kaibel, 1890, IG","Boeckh, Franz, 1853, CIG","Alessi, 1833, III. Giuseppe Alessi al chiarissimo segretario dell'instituto archeologico, salute.","Alessi, 1833, Scavi di Catania",[191,192,193,194],"Q2SBPG9F","TQMVHEVL","SRZQ4DSI","F986DASI",[196,197,198,22,27,31,199,200,201,202,200,203,102],"isic001293","funerary inscription",{"_":5},"catina","catania","sicilia","sicily","ancient greek",[],{"title":206,"body":207,"divs":208,"editions":227,"images":237,"handnote":238},"ISic001293. Funerary inscription","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ(εοῖς)\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ(αταχθονίοις)\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">Δάφνη\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">γλυ[κυ-]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>τάτη\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">χαῖρ[ε]\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">[ἔζη-]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>σας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔτη\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">τύχης\u003C/span> Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al6-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>ΟΣ̣ \u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">πεπ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">ΔΑΦΝΗ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">ΓΛΥ[..]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ΤΑΤΗ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">ΧΑΙΡ[.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>ΣΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al5-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">ΤΥΧΗΣ\u003C/span>Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al6-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>Ο.\u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">ΠΕΠ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after Alessi and Kaibel\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 2\">line.2: \u003Cspan>Alessi: ΓΛΥΚυ... and ΓΛΥκυ...\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 3\">line.3: \u003Cspan>[ἔζυ]|σας sic Alessi; ἔζη]|σας Franz; χαῖρ[ε ν’ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 4\">line.4: \u003Cspan>ἔτη [ὑπό Alessi\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 5\">line.5: \u003Cspan>N[εοκορύτ]|ος Alessi; Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος Franz\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 6\">line.6: \u003Cspan>πεπ[ρωμενυς sic Alessi; πεπ[οίηκεν Franz\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>To the Underworld Gods. Sweetest Daphne, farewell. You lived for … years. … of fortune …\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>This is an epitaph for a woman named Daphne, preceded by an invocation to the chthonic gods. The deceased is described with an attribute (ll. 2–3 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">γλυ[κυ]|τάτη\u003C/span>) that is quite common, followed by a greeting and the verb ζάω in the second person singular, with a direct address to the deceased made even more effective by the greeting formula. The age has been lost in a lacuna. The final part of the epitaph is very fragmentary: Kaibel suggests lines 5-6 likely to be consolatory epithets (e.g. \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τύχης ... πεπρωμεν\u003C/span>), rather than e.g. name of a male relative responsible for the building of the monument (as Alessi and Franz believed, since the first supplied at ll. 5-6 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ν[εοκορύτ]|ος πεπ[ρωμένυς\u003C/span>, the second at ll. 4-6 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος πεπ[οίηκεν\u003C/span>), and notes a suggestion of Willamowitz that the final part might have been in verse (iambic trimeter), and even the whole, if the age were a single syllable (e.g. \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Δάφνη γλυ[κυ]|τάτη χαῖρ[ε ν´ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη\u003C/span>).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Alessi 1833 226 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Alessi 1833 172 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Franz 1853 5703 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Kaibel 1890 \u003Ca href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">469\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence \u003C/div>",[209,212,215,218,221,224],{"id":210,"html":211},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ(εοῖς)\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ(αταχθονίοις)\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">Δάφνη\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">γλυ[κυ-]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>τάτη\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">χαῖρ[ε]\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">[ἔζη-]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>σας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔτη\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">τύχης\u003C/span> Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al6-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>ΟΣ̣ \u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">πεπ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">ΔΑΦΝΗ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">ΓΛΥ[..]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ΤΑΤΗ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">ΧΑΙΡ[.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>ΣΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al5-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">ΤΥΧΗΣ\u003C/span>Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al6-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>Ο.\u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">ΠΕΠ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":213,"html":214},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after Alessi and Kaibel\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 2\">line.2: \u003Cspan>Alessi: ΓΛΥΚυ... and ΓΛΥκυ...\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 3\">line.3: \u003Cspan>[ἔζυ]|σας sic Alessi; ἔζη]|σας Franz; χαῖρ[ε ν’ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 4\">line.4: \u003Cspan>ἔτη [ὑπό Alessi\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 5\">line.5: \u003Cspan>N[εοκορύτ]|ος Alessi; Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος Franz\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 6\">line.6: \u003Cspan>πεπ[ρωμενυς sic Alessi; πεπ[οίηκεν Franz\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":216,"html":217},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>To the Underworld Gods. Sweetest Daphne, farewell. You lived for … years. … of fortune …\u003C/p>  ",{"id":219,"html":220},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>This is an epitaph for a woman named Daphne, preceded by an invocation to the chthonic gods. The deceased is described with an attribute (ll. 2–3 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">γλυ[κυ]|τάτη\u003C/span>) that is quite common, followed by a greeting and the verb ζάω in the second person singular, with a direct address to the deceased made even more effective by the greeting formula. The age has been lost in a lacuna. The final part of the epitaph is very fragmentary: Kaibel suggests lines 5-6 likely to be consolatory epithets (e.g. \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τύχης ... πεπρωμεν\u003C/span>), rather than e.g. name of a male relative responsible for the building of the monument (as Alessi and Franz believed, since the first supplied at ll. 5-6 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ν[εοκορύτ]|ος πεπ[ρωμένυς\u003C/span>, the second at ll. 4-6 \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος πεπ[οίηκεν\u003C/span>), and notes a suggestion of Willamowitz that the final part might have been in verse (iambic trimeter), and even the whole, if the age were a single syllable (e.g. \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Δάφνη γλυ[κυ]|τάτη χαῖρ[ε ν´ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη\u003C/span>).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":222,"html":223},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Alessi 1833 226 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Alessi 1833 172 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Franz 1853 5703 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Kaibel 1890 \u003Ca href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">469\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":225,"html":226},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence ",[228,230,233,234],{"html":229},"Text encoding: Jonathan Prag",{"id":231,"lang":102,"html":232},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ(εοῖς)\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ(αταχθονίοις)\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">Δάφνη\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">γλυ[κυ-]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>τάτη\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">χαῖρ[ε]\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">[ἔζη-]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>σας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔτη\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">τύχης\u003C/span> Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al6-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>ΟΣ̣ \u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">πεπ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":229},{"id":235,"lang":102,"html":236},"edition-diplomatic","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">ΔΑΦΝΗ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">ΓΛΥ[..]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ΤΑΤΗ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"χαῖρε\">ΧΑΙΡ[.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>ΣΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al5-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"τύχης\">ΤΥΧΗΣ\u003C/span>Ν[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al6-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>Ο.\u003Cspan data-text=\"πεπ\">ΠΕΠ[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",[],[],"\u003C?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"https://epidoc.stoa.org/schema/latest/tei-epidoc.rng\" type=\"application/xml\" schematypens=\"http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"../schematron/ircyr-checking.sch\" schematypens=\"http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron\"?>\n\u003CTEI xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:xi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude\" xml:lang=\"en\">\n    \u003CteiHeader>\n        \u003CfileDesc>\n            \u003CtitleS